---
import { CLI_DOCS_URL, JJPR_URL } from "../config";
---

<section class="band" id="stacks">
  <div class="container split">
    <div class="copy prose">
      <h2>Stacks become pull requests</h2>
      <p>
        Publish pushes a stack to GitHub as one pull request per change, in landing order,
        and brings their bases and descriptions up to date each time you publish again.
        Follow checks and
        reviews in the app, land one round, or let auto-land merge the stack and rebase what
        is left while Jiji is open. Stacks made with <a href={JJPR_URL}>jjpr</a> are
        recognized as they are.
      </p>
      <p>
        The same engine runs in your terminal as <code>jiji</code>. Every stack command takes
        <code>--dry-run</code> and <code>--json</code>, so scripts and coding agents can
        publish and land too. <a href={CLI_DOCS_URL}>Read the CLI guide</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <pre class="term" aria-label="jiji command examples"><span class="prompt">$ </span>jiji status             <span class="note"># stack, PRs, landing readiness</span>
<span class="prompt">$ </span>jiji publish --dry-run  <span class="note"># preview pushes and PR updates</span>
<span class="prompt">$ </span>jiji publish --draft    <span class="note"># open new PRs as drafts</span>
<span class="prompt">$ </span>jiji ready              <span class="note"># mark them ready for review</span>
<span class="prompt">$ </span>jiji land               <span class="note"># land one round, reconcile</span>
<span class="prompt">$ </span>jiji watch              <span class="note"># auto-land until done</span></pre>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .split {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.05fr);
    gap: clamp(28px, 5vw, 64px);
    align-items: start;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: var(--fs-h2);
    margin-bottom: var(--sp-4);
  }

  .copy p {
    color: var(--clr-text-2);
  }

  .copy p + p {
    margin-top: var(--sp-4);
  }

  .term {
    margin-top: var(--sp-1);
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .split {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
